  {
   "name": "AuthoringNotes",
   "type": "comment",
   "node_position": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": -400
   },
   "parameters": {},
   "seed": 0,
   "seed_locked": true,
   "title": "Edit pigment and tissue response; preserve atlas registration",
   "size": {
    "x": 1400,
    "y": 300
   },
   "color": {
    "type": "Color",
    "r": 0.18,
    "g": 0.26,
    "b": 0.18,
    "a": 1
   },
   "text": "The retained pigment/cutout is the authored image dependency. Pigment tint/value and cutout bias are editable; defaults preserve its appearance/coverage subject to native storage quantization. Do not move atlas parts or resize crop atlases without updating their model/row coordinates. Where the runtime consumes normal/surface maps, SurfaceResponse rebuilds them from editable stock Gaussian, Math and normal primitives. Relief is an artistic estimate from encoded source detail/alpha, not measured shape recovered from color. It intentionally stays independent of pigment tint edits. Native spatial blur/half intermediates differ from the historical FFT recipe; earlier cutout numeric maps also used a legacy color resize, so no byte/appearance parity is claimed before native/game comparison. The output dimensions equal the source; internal Gaussian grids are power-of-two half-float, with radii expressed in source pixels. Final numeric encoding is only a PNG8 storage boundary; RGB pigment is not shifted. MegaMek/Maps exports existing runtime filenames only. Model impostors remain regenerated from actual model/material inputs by the existing tree baker; this graph is not a replacement for those view bakes."
  }
 ],
